<title>INDIA: RBI data on counrty-wise foreign direct investment.</title>
<headline>RBI data on counrty-wise foreign direct investment.</headline>
<text>
<p>Foreign Direct Investment Inflows</p>
<p>			     (Country-wise)</p>
<p>							  (US $ Million)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>		1995-96	 1994-95	1993-94     1992-93</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>U.S.A.	  192.4	   202.8	   98.8	  21.7</p>
<p>U.K.	     70.0	   143.5	   64.1	   6.6</p>
<p>Japan	    60.9	    95.0	   36.9	  25.7</p>
<p>Netherlands    49.8	    44.6	   46.5	  21.0</p>
<p>Germany	  99.2	    34.6	   35.1	  21.4</p>
<p>Switzerland    32.6	    26.2	   22.5	  35.3</p>
<p>Singapore	58.8	    24.5	    9.9	   2.8</p>
<p>HongKong	 98.5	    21.4	    6.1	   4.0</p>
<p>France	   62.7	    14.2	   10.4	   9.2</p>
<p>Others	  693.1	   265.3	   38.7	 132.2</p>
<p>Total	 1,418.0	   872.0	  369.0	 280.0</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Note : NRI direct investment routed through the Reserve Bank of India (RBI) has been excluded as country-wise details are not available.</p>
<p>Source : Reserve Bank of India annual report for 1995/96 (July-June).</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
